# ==============================================================================
# RMSM Docker Platform — root .dockerignore
# ==============================================================================
# Required by docker/build.Dockerfile's `COPY . .` (the one point in the
# platform where full repository source enters a build). Without this
# file, that COPY would also pull in every workspace's local node_modules
# (already resolved for the *host* machine's OS/arch, not the container's),
# .git history, and prior local build output — bloating the build context
# transferred to the daemon on every single build (directly working
# against "Fast Docker caching") and risking a stale host node_modules
# shadowing the fresh, container-native `pnpm install --offline` result
# produced inside build.Dockerfile.
#
# This file is intentionally scoped to Docker-context concerns only. It
# does not move, rename, or remove anything — every path listed here
# still exists on disk exactly as before; it is simply excluded from what
# gets sent to the Docker build context.
# ==============================================================================

# Dependency trees — reinstalled fresh, inside the container, by
# deps.Dockerfile / build.Dockerfile. Host-resolved node_modules must
# never be copied into an image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Version control — never needed inside an image, and .git alone can be
# larger than the entire application source.
.git
.gitignore

# Local build output — regenerated inside build.Dockerfile; stale host
# output must never shadow a container-built artifact.
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Prisma's generated client is produced fresh by build.Dockerfile's
# `prisma generate` step, not copied in from the host.
**/.prisma

# Editor/OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Local environment files — real secrets must never be baked into an
# image layer. Runtime configuration is injected via the orchestrator
# (Docker Compose env_file, Kubernetes Secrets/ConfigMaps), consistent
# with how packages/config's env loader already treats a committed .env
# as a local-development convenience, not a production source of truth.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Docker's own build context never needs to include itself recursively,
# and Phase 2's compose files are irrelevant to what these Dockerfiles
# build.
docker/scripts/**/*.md

# Test artifacts and logs.
**/*.log
**/junit.xml

# PNPM local store
.pnpm-store

# Additional build outputs
**/build
**/out
**/.cache

# Python caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv

# Archive files
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar